Add new media blocks before prefers-reduced-motion.

Mobile portrait specifics:
```
@media (max-width:520px){
  body.touch-mode .dialogue{bottom: calc(214px + safe); width: calc(100vw - 16px); ...}
  body.touch-mode .dlg-portrait{width:52px;height:64px}
  body.touch-mode .dlg-pt{font-size:10px}
  body.touch-mode .dlg-en{font-size:7.5px}
  body.touch-mode .dlg-next{min-width:44px}
  body.touch-mode .objective-panel{width:172px}
  body.touch-mode .mobile-status{top:calc(164px + safe)}
  body.touch-mode .touch-actions{transform:scale(.94);transform-origin:bottom right}
  body.touch-mode .touch-look-hint{display:none}
  body.touch-mode .tutorial{bottom:calc(224px + safe); ...}
}
```
Wait dialogue at bottom 214 overlaps status? Dialogue is width 96vw and bottom 214; it's above controls. Good. But subtitle bottom 206 also. Fine.

On 390x844: minimap 128 at top 8; status top 170; objective panel top 8 right 12. Status width ~165. Good.

The mobile status `top:170` may overlap the objective panel? Objective panel height ~70, top 8..78, no.

Touch brand at top center may overlap objective panel (starts x 188). Brand centered x 195 width ~80 => 155..235, overlaps objective x 188..378 at y 8..30. That's a conflict. Move touch-brand to bottom center? Or hide it. Better place at top-left under minimap? status there. Hide brand on small screens, or put at bottom center above joystick? Hmm. We can place it at `top: calc(8px + safe); left: 12px` but minimap occupies. Let's just hide `.touch-brand` on max-width 680 and landscape. On larger tablets, show top center. Or move brand to bottom center at `bottom: calc(8px + safe); left: 50%`; on 390, joystick and actions leave 26px gap, so brand would overlap. Hide on small.

Add `@media (max-width:680px){ body.touch-mode .touch-brand{display:none} }`.

Landscape:
```
@media (orientation:landscape) and (max-height:520px){
  body.touch-mode .minimap-wrap{width:104px;height:104px}
  body.touch-mode .hud-top-left{top:6px;left:10px}
  body.touch-mode .mobile-status{top:calc(118px + safe); left:10px; transform:scale(.88); transform-origin:top left}
  body.touch-mode .objective-panel{width:168px}
  body.touch-mode .joystick{width:100px;height:100px;left:12px;bottom:10px}
  body.touch-mode .touch-actions{transform:scale(.84); transform-origin:bottom right; right:6px; bottom:6px}
  body.touch-mode .dialogue{bottom:calc(8px + safe); width:min(640px,80vw); left:50%}
  ...
}
```
But dialogue at bottom center may overlap controls; in landscape, controls are at sides, center free. width 60vw. Fine. Actually the dialogue is 880 wide; set width 56vw and bottom 8. It may overlap joystick at left if width too wide; 56vw of 844 = 472, centered x 186..658, joystick x 12..112, actions x ~? right 6 + 216*.84=181 => x 657..838. Just fits. Good.

Need also `.touch-look-hint` position right center might overlap actions; hide.

Also `body.touch-mode .subtitle{bottom:...}` for landscape maybe 100px.

Let's add.

