412:.touch-brand{position:absolute;top:calc(8px + env(safe-area-inset-top));left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:rgba(234,242,242,.55);pointer-events:none;white-space:nowrap}
413:.touch-brand span{display:block;font-family:var(--font-ui);font-size:5px;letter-spacing:.28em;color:var(--teal);text-align:center;margin-top:1px;font-weight:800}
484:body.touch-mode .touch-brand{display:none}
970:  body.touch-mode .touch-brand{display:none}
1007:  body.touch-mode .touch-brand{display:none}

Line 484 hide always. Change to display none by default, then add media min-width 900 show? But touch mode on tablet maybe. Let's replace line 484 with:
```
body.touch-mode .touch-brand{display:none}
@media (min-width:900px){body.touch-mode .touch-brand{display:block}}
```
But later media queries at 970/1007 hide again for <=680/landscape. Fine. Add after.

