Now responsive media queries for D-pad/shoulders. Existing @media max-width 680 and 390 and landscape. Add rules. Let's edit each block.

At max-width 680 block, add:
```
body.touch-mode .touch-shoulders-left{bottom:calc(248px + safe);}
body.touch-mode .touch-dpad{bottom:calc(146px + safe);}
body.touch-mode .touch-mini{width:34px;height:34px}
```
At max-width 390:
```
body.touch-mode .touch-shoulders-left{bottom:calc(238px + safe);}
body.touch-mode .touch-dpad{bottom:calc(140px + safe);width:94px;height:94px}
body.touch-mode .dpad-btn{width:32px;height:32px}
positions adjust (up left 31, left top31, etc.)
```
Maybe simpler use transform scale .94 for dpad and shoulders. But positions based on 100 size; scaling container works. Add `transform:scale(calc(var(--touch-scale,1)*.94))`. Fine.

Landscape max-height 540:
```
body.touch-mode .touch-shoulders-left{bottom:calc(228px + safe);}
body.touch-mode .touch-dpad{bottom:calc(122px + safe);}
```
Also joystick bottom 10, actions bottom 6. L1/L2 bottom 228, D-pad bottom 122. Good.
At 680 width portrait, existing joystick 108? Actually max-width 390 sets 108; max-width 680 doesn't. Fine.

